Chapter: Monopoly
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter Random

 We say:

Section: The Rules

 The rules as Hasbro publishes them (Monopoly, the US edition's rules
 leaflet, with the amounts of the 2008 edition onward).

 Rule 1. Each player starts on GO with $1500. The Bank holds every deed,
 32 houses and 12 hotels.

 Rule 2. A turn is a throw of two dice and a move clockwise by their total.
 A player who throws doubles obeys the square and throws again; the third
 doubles in one turn goes straight to Jail without moving, and the turn
 ends.

 Rule 3. Passing or landing on GO pays $200, by a throw or by a card.

 Rule 4. A player landing on an unowned deed may buy it at its printed
 price. A deed not bought is auctioned by the Bank at once to every player,
 the one who declined included, starting at any price; the highest bidder
 buys it.

 Rule 5. Rent. A lot charges its deed's rent, doubled while it has no
 buildings and its owner holds the whole colour group, even when another
 lot of the group is mortgaged; a lot with houses or a hotel charges the
 deed's rent for them. A railroad charges 25, 50, 100 or 200 as its owner
 holds 1, 2, 3 or 4 railroads. A utility charges 4 times the dice thrown
 when its owner holds one utility and 10 times when both. A mortgaged deed
 charges nothing, and an owner in Jail still collects.

 Rule 6. Building. The owner of a whole colour group, no lot of it
 mortgaged, may buy houses from the Bank at the deed's house price, and
 must build evenly: no lot takes a second house before every lot of the
 group has one, and so on to four. The fifth is a hotel, for which the
 lot's four houses go back to the Bank. Houses are bought only while the
 Bank has one, and hotels likewise. Buildings sell back to the Bank at half
 their price, evenly, a hotel coming back as four houses.

 Rule 7. Mortgages. An unimproved deed mortgages to the Bank for half its
 price, once every building on its colour group is sold. The mortgage is
 lifted by paying that sum plus 10% interest.

 Rule 8. Income Tax (square 4) is $200 and Luxury Tax (square 38) $100.
 Free Parking and Just Visiting do nothing.

 Rule 9. Chance (squares 7, 22, 36) and Community Chest (2, 17, 33): the
 top card is drawn, obeyed and put at the bottom. A Get Out of Jail Free
 card is kept until used and then goes to the bottom of its deck.

 Chance: 0 advance to Boardwalk; 1 advance to GO; 2 advance to Illinois
 Avenue; 3 advance to St. Charles Place; 4 and 5 advance to the nearest
 railroad, bought if unowned, and if owned pay its owner twice the rent; 6
 advance to the nearest utility, bought if unowned, and if owned throw the
 dice and pay its owner ten times the throw; 7 the Bank pays a $50
 dividend; 8 Get Out of Jail Free; 9 go back three squares; 10 go to Jail;
 11 general repairs, $25 a house and $100 a hotel; 12 speeding fine $15; 13
 advance to Reading Railroad; 14 chairman of the board, pay every other
 player $50; 15 building loan matures, collect $150.

 Community Chest: 0 advance to GO; 1 bank error, collect $200; 2 doctor's
 fee $50; 3 sale of stock, collect $50; 4 Get Out of Jail Free; 5 go to
 Jail; 6 holiday fund, collect $100; 7 income tax refund, collect $20; 8
 birthday, collect $10 from every other player; 9 life insurance, collect
 $100; 10 hospital fees $100; 11 school fees $50; 12 consultancy fee,
 collect $25; 13 street repairs, $40 a house and $115 a hotel; 14 beauty
 contest, collect $10; 15 inherit $100.

 Rule 10. Jail. A player goes to Jail from the Go To Jail square, from a
 card or on the third doubles, and the turn ends. A player in Jail leaves
 by throwing doubles on any of the next three turns, moving by that throw
 with no throw again; by using a Get Out of Jail Free card; or by paying
 $50 before throwing on either of the next two turns. After the third
 failed throw the player pays $50 and moves by that throw.

 Rule 11. Debt. A player owing more than their cash raises it by selling
 buildings and mortgaging, and a player who cannot is bankrupt. Bankrupt
 to a player: the buildings are sold to the Bank at half price and the
 creditor takes the cash, the deeds and the cards, paying the Bank 10%
 interest on each mortgaged deed at once. Bankrupt to the Bank: the
 buildings return to the Bank, the deeds are auctioned unmortgaged, and the
 cards go back to their decks.

 Rule 12. Deeds change hands between players by agreement, but not a deed
 whose colour group carries a building.

 Rule 13. The last player not bankrupt wins.

 Where the rules leave a choice, this engine takes these. An auction goes
 round the table from the player whose turn it is; each in turn bids more
 than the standing bid, at most their cash, or drops out for good, and the
 last left holding a bid buys; nobody bidding leaves the deed with the
 Bank. Buildings, mortgages and lifts happen while a turn waits to throw,
 to buy or to pay, not during an auction or an open trade offer. A hotel
 sold while the Bank has fewer than four houses comes back as the houses
 the Bank has, and the rest sell with it. Interest and the lifting price
 round up to the dollar. Several debts from one card are owed in seat
 order from the player whose turn it is. A game nobody has won after 600
 turns goes to the player of greatest worth: cash, deeds at their price or
 half when mortgaged, and buildings at their price.

Section: Types

  MonopolyState = record {
    cells : List Integer
  }

  MonopolyResult = record {
    winner     : Integer,
    turns      : Integer,
    final-cash : List Integer
  }

Section: The State Layout

 The state is one Integer list of 472 slots. Slots 0 to 26 are the fields
 named below. Each deck is a length and 16 card slots, Chance at 30 and
 Community Chest at 50. The auction's bidders sit at 70, one flag a seat.
 The debt queue is a length at 80 and up to 64 triples of debtor, creditor
 (-1 is the Bank) and amount. The Bank's auction queue is a length at 280
 and up to 28 deeds. Players sit at 320 in strides of 8 (square, cash, in
 Jail, failed throws in Jail, Chance card, Community Chest card,
 bankrupt); deeds at 360 in strides of 4 (owner, buildings with 5 a hotel,
 mortgaged, asked for in trade this turn).

  mono-f-np : Integer
  mono-f-np = 0

  mono-f-cur : Integer
  mono-f-cur = 1

  mono-f-turn : Integer
  mono-f-turn = 2

  mono-f-over : Integer
  mono-f-over = 3

  mono-f-winner : Integer
  mono-f-winner = 4

  mono-f-phase : Integer
  mono-f-phase = 5

  mono-f-pending : Integer
  mono-f-pending = 6

  mono-f-roll : Integer
  mono-f-roll = 7

  mono-f-d1 : Integer
  mono-f-d1 = 8

  mono-f-d2 : Integer
  mono-f-d2 = 9

  mono-f-doubles : Integer
  mono-f-doubles = 10

  mono-f-again : Integer
  mono-f-again = 11

  mono-f-houses : Integer
  mono-f-houses = 12

  mono-f-hotels : Integer
  mono-f-hotels = 13

  mono-f-human : Integer
  mono-f-human = 14

  mono-f-aprop : Integer
  mono-f-aprop = 15

  mono-f-ahigh : Integer
  mono-f-ahigh = 16

  mono-f-alead : Integer
  mono-f-alead = 17

  mono-f-aact : Integer
  mono-f-aact = 18

  mono-f-twant : Integer
  mono-f-twant = 19

  mono-f-tgive : Integer
  mono-f-tgive = 20

  mono-f-tprice : Integer
  mono-f-tprice = 21

  mono-f-move : Integer
  mono-f-move = 23

  mono-f-seed : Integer
  mono-f-seed = 24

  mono-f-cthrow : Integer
  mono-f-cthrow = 25

  mono-f-card : Integer
  mono-f-card = 26

  mono-size : Integer
  mono-size = 472

  mono-deck-at : Integer -> Integer
  mono-deck-at (d) = 30 + d * 20

  mono-debt-at : Integer
  mono-debt-at = 80

  mono-aq-at : Integer
  mono-aq-at = 280

  mono-pslot : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-pslot (p) (f) = 320 + p * 8 + f

  mono-dslot : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-dslot (pi) (f) = 360 + pi * 4 + f

 Phases: 0 waiting to throw, 1 a deed offered, 2 a trade offered to the
 person, 3 an auction, 4 a debt short of cash, 5 over.

 Actions: 0 throw, 1 buy, 2 decline, 3 bid, 4 drop out, 5 build, 6 sell a
 building, 7 mortgage, 8 lift a mortgage, 9 pay the Jail fine, 10 use a
 Get Out of Jail Free card, 11 declare bankruptcy, 12 accept a trade, 13
 refuse it, 14 propose one.

Section: Reading And Writing

  mono-get : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-get (s) (i) = list-at (s.cells) i

  mono-put : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-put (s) (i) (v) =
    let c = list-set-at (s.cells) i v
    in s

  mono-copy : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-copy (s) = MonopolyState { cells = mono-copy-cells (s.cells) 0 (list-length (s.cells)) [] }

  mono-copy-cells : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mono-copy-cells (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else mono-copy-cells xs (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  mono-players : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-players (s) = mono-get s mono-f-np

  mono-cur : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-cur (s) = mono-get s mono-f-cur

  mono-phase : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-phase (s) = mono-get s mono-f-phase

  mono-over : MonopolyState -> Boolean
  mono-over (s) = mono-get s mono-f-over == 1

  mono-set-phase : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-set-phase (s) (ph) = mono-put s mono-f-phase ph

  mono-pos : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-pos (s) (p) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p 0)

  mono-cash : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-cash (s) (p) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p 1)

  mono-jailed : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-jailed (s) (p) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p 2) == 1

  mono-jail-turns : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-jail-turns (s) (p) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p 3)

  mono-cards : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-cards (s) (p) (d) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p (4 + d))

  mono-out : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-out (s) (p) = mono-get s (mono-pslot p 6) == 1

  mono-owner : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-owner (s) (pi) = mono-get s (mono-dslot pi 0)

  mono-houses : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-houses (s) (pi) = mono-get s (mono-dslot pi 1)

  mono-mortgaged : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-mortgaged (s) (pi) = mono-get s (mono-dslot pi 2) == 1

  mono-asked : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-asked (s) (pi) = mono-get s (mono-dslot pi 3) == 1

  mono-add-cash : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-add-cash (s) (p) (n) =
    if p < 0 then s else mono-put s (mono-pslot p 1) (mono-cash s p + n)

Section: The Deeds

 A deed row: board square, price, rent unimproved and with 1 to 4 houses
 and a hotel, house price, group. Groups 0 to 7 are the colours from
 Mediterranean to Boardwalk, 8 the railroads and 9 the utilities.

  mono-pick : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-pick (k) (a0) (a1) (a2) (a3) (a4) (a5) (a6) (a7) (a8) (a9) =
    if k == 0 then a0
    else if k == 1 then a1
    else if k == 2 then a2
    else if k == 3 then a3
    else if k == 4 then a4
    else if k == 5 then a5
    else if k == 6 then a6
    else if k == 7 then a7
    else if k == 8 then a8
    else a9

  mono-deed : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-deed (pi) (k) =
    when pi
      is 0 -> mono-pick k 1 60 2 10 30 90 160 250 50 0
      is 1 -> mono-pick k 3 60 4 20 60 180 320 450 50 0
      is 2 -> mono-pick k 5 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 8
      is 3 -> mono-pick k 6 100 6 30 90 270 400 550 50 1
      is 4 -> mono-pick k 8 100 6 30 90 270 400 550 50 1
      is 5 -> mono-pick k 9 120 8 40 100 300 450 600 50 1
      is 6 -> mono-pick k 11 140 10 50 150 450 625 750 100 2
      is 7 -> mono-pick k 12 150 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 9
      is 8 -> mono-pick k 13 140 10 50 150 450 625 750 100 2
      is 9 -> mono-pick k 14 160 12 60 180 500 700 900 100 2
      is 10 -> mono-pick k 15 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 8
      is 11 -> mono-pick k 16 180 14 70 200 550 750 950 100 3
      is 12 -> mono-pick k 18 180 14 70 200 550 750 950 100 3
      is 13 -> mono-pick k 19 200 16 80 220 600 800 1000 100 3
      is 14 -> mono-pick k 21 220 18 90 250 700 875 1050 150 4
      is 15 -> mono-pick k 23 220 18 90 250 700 875 1050 150 4
      is 16 -> mono-pick k 24 240 20 100 300 750 925 1100 150 4
      is 17 -> mono-pick k 25 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 8
      is 18 -> mono-pick k 26 260 22 110 330 800 975 1150 150 5
      is 19 -> mono-pick k 27 260 22 110 330 800 975 1150 150 5
      is 20 -> mono-pick k 28 150 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 9
      is 21 -> mono-pick k 29 280 24 120 360 850 1025 1200 150 5
      is 22 -> mono-pick k 31 300 26 130 390 900 1100 1275 200 6
      is 23 -> mono-pick k 32 300 26 130 390 900 1100 1275 200 6
      is 24 -> mono-pick k 34 320 28 150 450 1000 1200 1400 200 6
      is 25 -> mono-pick k 35 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 8
      is 26 -> mono-pick k 37 350 35 175 500 1100 1300 1500 200 7
      is 27 -> mono-pick k 39 400 50 200 600 1400 1700 2000 200 7
      is otherwise -> 0

  mono-deeds : Integer
  mono-deeds = 28

  mono-space : Integer -> Integer
  mono-space (pi) = mono-deed pi 0

  mono-price : Integer -> Integer
  mono-price (pi) = mono-deed pi 1

  mono-house-cost : Integer -> Integer
  mono-house-cost (pi) = mono-deed pi 8

  mono-group : Integer -> Integer
  mono-group (pi) = mono-deed pi 9

  mono-mortgage-value : Integer -> Integer
  mono-mortgage-value (pi) = mono-price pi / 2

  mono-lift-cost : Integer -> Integer
  mono-lift-cost (pi) = (mono-mortgage-value pi * 11 + 9) / 10

  mono-interest : Integer -> Integer
  mono-interest (pi) = (mono-mortgage-value pi + 9) / 10

  mono-prop-at : Integer -> Integer
  mono-prop-at (sq) = mono-prop-at-loop sq 0

  mono-prop-at-loop : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-prop-at-loop (sq) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then (-1)
    else if mono-space pi == sq then pi
    else mono-prop-at-loop sq (pi + 1)

  mono-group-size : Integer -> Integer
  mono-group-size (g) =
    if g == 0 then 2
    else if g == 7 then 2
    else if g == 8 then 4
    else if g == 9 then 2
    else 3

Section: Colour Groups

  mono-group-held : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-group-held (s) (p) (g) = mono-held-loop s p g 0 0

  mono-held-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-held-loop (s) (p) (g) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else let hit = if mono-group pi == g then (if mono-owner s pi == p then 1 else 0) else 0
    in mono-held-loop s p g (pi + 1) (acc + hit)

  mono-holds-group : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-holds-group (s) (p) (g) = mono-group-held s p g == mono-group-size g

  mono-group-min : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-group-min (s) (g) = mono-min-loop s g 0 9

  mono-min-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-min-loop (s) (g) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else if mono-group pi /= g then mono-min-loop s g (pi + 1) acc
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in mono-min-loop s g (pi + 1) (if h < acc then h else acc)

  mono-group-max : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-group-max (s) (g) = mono-max-loop s g 0 0

  mono-max-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-max-loop (s) (g) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else if mono-group pi /= g then mono-max-loop s g (pi + 1) acc
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in mono-max-loop s g (pi + 1) (if h > acc then h else acc)

  mono-group-mortgages : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-group-mortgages (s) (g) = mono-mortgages-loop s g 0 0

  mono-mortgages-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-mortgages-loop (s) (g) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else let hit = if mono-group pi == g then (if mono-mortgaged s pi then 1 else 0) else 0
    in mono-mortgages-loop s g (pi + 1) (acc + hit)

Section: Rent

  mono-rr-rent : Integer -> Integer
  mono-rr-rent (n) =
    if n <= 1 then 25
    else if n == 2 then 50
    else if n == 3 then 100
    else 200

  mono-rent : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-rent (s) (pi) (mode) =
    let o = mono-owner s pi
    in let g = mono-group pi
    in if mono-mortgaged s pi then 0
    else if g == 8 then mono-rr-rent (mono-group-held s o 8) * (if mode == 1 then 2 else 1)
    else if g == 9 then mono-utility-rent s o mode
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in if h > 0 then mono-deed pi (2 + h)
    else if mono-holds-group s o g then 2 * mono-deed pi 2
    else mono-deed pi 2

  mono-utility-rent : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-utility-rent (s) (o) (mode) =
    if mode == 2 then 10 * mono-get s mono-f-cthrow
    else if mono-group-held s o 9 == 2 then 10 * mono-get s mono-f-roll
    else 4 * mono-get s mono-f-roll

Section: Dice

 The Rng's low bit alternates from one state to the next, so two dice drawn
 from consecutive states never match and doubles never come; each die here
 folds the high bits of its own mix down instead.

  mono-die : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-die (seed) (k) = 1 + rng-mod (bit-shru (mix-bits seed k) 1) 6

  mono-card-throw : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-card-throw (s) =
    let seed = mono-get s mono-f-seed
    in mono-die seed 3 + mono-die seed 4

Section: Setting Up

  mono-zeros : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mono-zeros (n) (acc) =
    if n <= 0 then acc
    else mono-zeros (n - 1) (list-push acc 0)

  mono-init : Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-init (seed) (num-players) =
    let np = if num-players < 2 then 2 else if num-players > 4 then 4 else num-players
    in let s0 = MonopolyState { cells = mono-zeros mono-size [] }
    in let s1 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s0 mono-f-np np) mono-f-winner (-1)) mono-f-pending (-1)
    in let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s1 mono-f-houses 32) mono-f-hotels 12) mono-f-human (-1)
    in let s3 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-f-aprop (-1)) mono-f-alead (-1)) mono-f-aact (-1)
    in let s4 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s3 mono-f-twant (-1)) mono-f-tgive (-1)) mono-f-card (-1)
    in let s5 = mono-init-players s4 0 np
    in let s6 = mono-init-deeds s5 0
    in mono-shuffle (mono-shuffle (mono-init-deck (mono-init-deck s6 0) 1) seed 0 15) seed 1 15

  mono-set-human : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-set-human (s) (p) = mono-put s mono-f-human p

  mono-init-players : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-init-players (s) (p) (np) =
    if p >= np then s
    else mono-init-players (mono-put s (mono-pslot p 1) 1500) (p + 1) np

  mono-init-deeds : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-init-deeds (s) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then s
    else mono-init-deeds (mono-put s (mono-dslot pi 0) (-1)) (pi + 1)

  mono-init-deck : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-init-deck (s) (d) = mono-fill-deck (mono-put s (mono-deck-at d) 16) d 0

  mono-fill-deck : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-fill-deck (s) (d) (k) =
    if k >= 16 then s
    else mono-fill-deck (mono-put s (mono-deck-at d + 1 + k) k) d (k + 1)

  mono-shuffle : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-shuffle (s) (seed) (d) (i) =
    if i <= 0 then s
    else let j = rng-mod (bit-shru (mix-bits seed (100 + d * 16 + i)) 1) (i + 1)
    in let base = mono-deck-at d + 1
    in let a = mono-get s (base + i)
    in let b = mono-get s (base + j)
    in mono-shuffle (mono-put (mono-put s (base + i) b) (base + j) a) seed d (i - 1)

Section: Decks

  mono-deck-len : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-deck-len (s) (d) = mono-get s (mono-deck-at d)

  mono-deck-card : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-deck-card (s) (d) (k) = mono-get s (mono-deck-at d + 1 + k)

  mono-goojf : Integer -> Integer
  mono-goojf (d) = if d == 0 then 8 else 4

  mono-deck-pop : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-deck-pop (s) (d) = mono-put (mono-shift-deck s d 0 (mono-deck-len s d)) (mono-deck-at d) (mono-deck-len s d - 1)

  mono-shift-deck : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-shift-deck (s) (d) (k) (n) =
    if k + 1 >= n then s
    else mono-shift-deck (mono-put s (mono-deck-at d + 1 + k) (mono-deck-card s d (k + 1))) d (k + 1) n

  mono-deck-bottom : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-deck-bottom (s) (d) (card) =
    let n = mono-deck-len s d
    in mono-put (mono-put s (mono-deck-at d + 1 + n) card) (mono-deck-at d) (n + 1)

Section: Debts

  mono-debts : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-debts (s) = mono-get s mono-debt-at

  mono-debt : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-debt (s) (k) (f) = mono-get s (mono-debt-at + 1 + k * 3 + f)

  mono-owe : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-owe (s) (d) (c) (amt) =
    let n = mono-debts s
    in if amt <= 0 then s
    else if n >= 64 then s
    else let at = mono-debt-at + 1 + n * 3
    in mono-put (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s at d) (at + 1) c) (at + 2) amt) mono-debt-at (n + 1)

 A debt queue is compacted in place: entry k moves to slot j when every
 entry before it that was kept sits below j.

  mono-debt-filter : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-debt-filter (s) (drop) (k) (j) (n) =
    if k >= n then mono-put s mono-debt-at j
    else let d = mono-debt s k 0
    in let c = mono-debt s k 1
    in let a = mono-debt s k 2
    in let gone = if k == 0 then drop == (-2) else False
    in if gone | d == drop | c == drop then mono-debt-filter s drop (k + 1) j n
    else let at = mono-debt-at + 1 + j * 3
    in mono-debt-filter (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s at d) (at + 1) c) (at + 2) a) drop (k + 1) (j + 1) n

  mono-debt-pop : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-debt-pop (s) = mono-debt-filter s (-2) 0 0 (mono-debts s)

  mono-drop-debts : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-drop-debts (s) (p) = mono-debt-filter s p 0 0 (mono-debts s)

  mono-aq : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-aq (s) = mono-get s mono-aq-at

  mono-aq-push : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-aq-push (s) (pi) =
    let n = mono-aq s
    in mono-put (mono-put s (mono-aq-at + 1 + n) pi) mono-aq-at (n + 1)

  mono-aq-pop : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-aq-pop (s) = mono-put (mono-aq-shift s 0 (mono-aq s)) mono-aq-at (mono-aq s - 1)

  mono-aq-shift : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-aq-shift (s) (k) (n) =
    if k + 1 >= n then s
    else mono-aq-shift (mono-put s (mono-aq-at + 1 + k) (mono-get s (mono-aq-at + 2 + k))) (k + 1) n

Section: Seats

  mono-live-count : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-live-count (s) (p) (acc) =
    if p >= mono-players s then acc
    else mono-live-count s (p + 1) (acc + (if mono-out s p then 0 else 1))

  mono-first-live : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-first-live (s) (p) =
    if p >= mono-players s then (-1)
    else if mono-out s p then mono-first-live s (p + 1)
    else p

  mono-next-seat : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-next-seat (s) (p) = mono-next-seat-loop s p 1

  mono-next-seat-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-next-seat-loop (s) (p) (k) =
    if k > mono-players s then p
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (mono-players s)
    in if mono-out s q then mono-next-seat-loop s p (k + 1)
    else q

  mono-actor : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-actor (s) =
    let ph = mono-phase s
    in if mono-over s then (-1)
    else if ph <= 1 then mono-cur s
    else if ph == 2 then mono-owner s (mono-get s mono-f-twant)
    else if ph == 3 then mono-get s mono-f-aact
    else if ph == 4 then mono-debt s 0 0
    else (-1)

Section: What Each Player May Do

  mono-live : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-live (s) (p) =
    if mono-over s then False
    else if p < 0 then False
    else if p >= mono-players s then False
    else if mono-out s p then False
    else True

  mono-asset-phase : MonopolyState -> Boolean
  mono-asset-phase (s) =
    let ph = mono-phase s
    in ph == 0 | ph == 1 | ph == 4

  mono-deed-ok : Integer -> Boolean
  mono-deed-ok (pi) = if pi < 0 then False else pi < mono-deeds

  mono-can-build : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-can-build (s) (p) (pi) =
    if mono-deed-ok pi == False then False
    else let g = mono-group pi
    in if g >= 8 then False
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then False
    else if mono-holds-group s p g == False then False
    else if mono-group-mortgages s g > 0 then False
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in if h >= 5 then False
    else if h > mono-group-min s g then False
    else if h == 4 then (if mono-get s mono-f-hotels < 1 then False else mono-cash s p >= mono-house-cost pi)
    else if mono-get s mono-f-houses < 1 then False
    else mono-cash s p >= mono-house-cost pi

  mono-can-sell : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-can-sell (s) (p) (pi) =
    if mono-deed-ok pi == False then False
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then False
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in if h < 1 then False
    else h == mono-group-max s (mono-group pi)

  mono-can-mortgage : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-can-mortgage (s) (p) (pi) =
    if mono-deed-ok pi == False then False
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then False
    else if mono-mortgaged s pi then False
    else if mono-group pi >= 8 then True
    else mono-group-max s (mono-group pi) == 0

  mono-can-lift : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-can-lift (s) (p) (pi) =
    if mono-deed-ok pi == False then False
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then False
    else if mono-mortgaged s pi == False then False
    else mono-cash s p >= mono-lift-cost pi

 What a player could raise by selling every building and mortgaging every
 deed. A hotel sells as five buildings whatever the Bank holds, because the
 houses it cannot come back as sell with it.

  mono-raisable : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-raisable (s) (p) = mono-raisable-loop s p 0 0

  mono-raisable-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-raisable-loop (s) (p) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then mono-raisable-loop s p (pi + 1) acc
    else let b = mono-houses s pi * (mono-house-cost pi / 2)
    in let m = if mono-mortgaged s pi then 0 else mono-mortgage-value pi
    in mono-raisable-loop s p (pi + 1) (acc + b + m)

  mono-legal : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-legal (s) (p) (kind) (arg) =
    if mono-live s p == False then False
    else let ph = mono-phase s
    in let mine = p == mono-cur s
    in if kind == 0 then (ph == 0) & mine
    else if kind == 1 then (if (ph == 1) & mine then mono-cash s p >= mono-price (mono-get s mono-f-pending) else False)
    else if kind == 2 then (ph == 1) & mine
    else if kind == 3 then (if (ph == 3) & (p == mono-get s mono-f-aact) then (arg > mono-get s mono-f-ahigh) & (arg <= mono-cash s p) else False)
    else if kind == 4 then (ph == 3) & (p == mono-get s mono-f-aact)
    else if kind == 5 then (if mono-asset-phase s then mono-can-build s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 6 then (if mono-asset-phase s then mono-can-sell s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 7 then (if mono-asset-phase s then mono-can-mortgage s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 8 then (if mono-asset-phase s then mono-can-lift s p arg else False)
    else if kind == 9 then (if (ph == 0) & mine & mono-jailed s p then (mono-jail-turns s p < 2) & (mono-cash s p >= 50) else False)
    else if kind == 10 then (if (ph == 0) & mine & mono-jailed s p then mono-cards s p 0 + mono-cards s p 1 > 0 else False)
    else if kind == 11 then (if (ph == 4) & (p == mono-debt s 0 0) then mono-cash s p + mono-raisable s p < mono-debt s 0 2 else False)
    else if kind == 12 then (ph == 2) & (p == mono-actor s)
    else if kind == 13 then (ph == 2) & (p == mono-actor s)
    else if kind == 14 then (if (ph == 0) & mine then mono-trade-ok s p arg else False)
    else False

Section: Acting

  mono-act : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-act (s) (p) (kind) (arg) =
    if mono-legal s p kind arg then mono-act-in (mono-copy s) p kind arg else s

 The unchecked form writes into the state it is given.

  mono-act-in : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-act-in (s) (p) (kind) (arg) =
    if kind == 0 then mono-roll s arg
    else if kind == 1 then mono-buy s p
    else if kind == 2 then mono-start-auction s (mono-get s mono-f-pending)
    else if kind == 3 then mono-bid s p arg
    else if kind == 4 then mono-drop s p
    else if kind == 5 then mono-after-asset (mono-build s p arg)
    else if kind == 6 then mono-after-asset (mono-sell s p arg)
    else if kind == 7 then mono-after-asset (mono-mortgage s p arg)
    else if kind == 8 then mono-after-asset (mono-lift s p arg)
    else if kind == 9 then mono-release (mono-add-cash s p (0 - 50)) p
    else if kind == 10 then mono-use-card s p
    else if kind == 11 then mono-continue (mono-bankrupt s p (mono-debt s 0 1))
    else if kind == 12 then mono-accept s
    else if kind == 13 then mono-clear-offer s
    else if kind == 14 then mono-trade s p arg
    else s

  mono-after-asset : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-after-asset (s) = if mono-phase s == 4 then mono-continue s else s

  mono-after : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-after (s) = if mono-phase s == 1 then s else mono-continue s

Section: The Throw

  mono-roll : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-roll (s) (seed) =
    let p = mono-cur s
    in let d1 = mono-die seed 1
    in let d2 = mono-die seed 2
    in let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-d1 d1) mono-f-d2 d2) mono-f-roll (d1 + d2)) mono-f-seed seed
    in if mono-jailed s2 p then mono-roll-jailed s2 p (d1 == d2) (d1 + d2)
    else if d1 == d2 then mono-roll-doubles s2 p (d1 + d2)
    else mono-after (mono-move-by (mono-put s2 mono-f-again 0) p (d1 + d2))

  mono-roll-doubles : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-roll-doubles (s) (p) (n) =
    let k = mono-get s mono-f-doubles + 1
    in if k >= 3 then mono-continue (mono-to-jail s p)
    else mono-after (mono-move-by (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-doubles k) mono-f-again 1) p n)

  mono-roll-jailed : MonopolyState, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-roll-jailed (s) (p) (doubles) (n) =
    let s2 = mono-put s mono-f-again 0
    in if doubles then mono-after (mono-move-by (mono-release s2 p) p n)
    else let t = mono-jail-turns s2 p + 1
    in if t >= 3 then mono-continue (mono-put (mono-owe (mono-release s2 p) p (-1) 50) mono-f-move n)
    else mono-continue (mono-put s2 (mono-pslot p 3) t)

  mono-release : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-release (s) (p) = mono-put (mono-put s (mono-pslot p 2) 0) (mono-pslot p 3) 0

  mono-to-jail : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-to-jail (s) (p) =
    let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s (mono-pslot p 0) 10) (mono-pslot p 2) 1) (mono-pslot p 3) 0
    in mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-f-again 0) mono-f-doubles 0

  mono-use-card : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-use-card (s) (p) =
    let d = if mono-cards s p 0 > 0 then 0 else 1
    in let s2 = mono-put s (mono-pslot p (4 + d)) 0
    in mono-release (mono-deck-bottom s2 d (mono-goojf d)) p

Section: Moving

  mono-move-by : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-move-by (s) (p) (n) =
    let from = mono-pos s p
    in let dest = rng-mod (from + n) 40
    in let s2 = if from + n >= 40 then mono-add-cash s p 200 else s
    in mono-land (mono-put s2 (mono-pslot p 0) dest) p dest 0

  mono-advance-to : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-advance-to (s) (p) (dest) (mode) =
    let s2 = if dest < mono-pos s p then mono-add-cash s p 200 else s
    in mono-land (mono-put s2 (mono-pslot p 0) dest) p dest mode

  mono-nearest : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-nearest (from) (g) =
    if g == 8 then (if from < 5 then 5 else if from < 15 then 15 else if from < 25 then 25 else if from < 35 then 35 else 5)
    else if from < 12 then 12
    else if from < 28 then 28
    else 12

 Mode 0 is an ordinary landing, 1 a card's railroad at double rent, 2 a
 card's utility at ten times a fresh throw.

  mono-land : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-land (s) (p) (sq) (mode) =
    if sq == 30 then mono-to-jail s p
    else if sq == 4 then mono-owe s p (-1) 200
    else if sq == 38 then mono-owe s p (-1) 100
    else if sq == 7 | sq == 22 | sq == 36 then mono-draw s p 0
    else if sq == 2 | sq == 17 | sq == 33 then mono-draw s p 1
    else let pi = mono-prop-at sq
    in if pi < 0 then s
    else mono-land-deed s p pi mode

  mono-land-deed : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-land-deed (s) (p) (pi) (mode) =
    let o = mono-owner s pi
    in if o < 0 then mono-set-phase (mono-put s mono-f-pending pi) 1
    else if o == p then s
    else if mono-mortgaged s pi then s
    else let s2 = if mode == 2 then mono-put s mono-f-cthrow (mono-card-throw s) else s
    in mono-owe s2 p o (mono-rent s2 pi mode)

Section: Cards

  mono-draw : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-draw (s) (p) (d) =
    let card = mono-deck-card s d 0
    in let s2 = mono-put (mono-deck-pop s d) mono-f-card (d * 16 + card)
    in if card == mono-goojf d then mono-put s2 (mono-pslot p (4 + d)) 1
    else if d == 0 then mono-chance (mono-deck-bottom s2 d card) p card
    else mono-chest (mono-deck-bottom s2 d card) p card

  mono-chance : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-chance (s) (p) (c) =
    if c == 0 then mono-advance-to s p 39 0
    else if c == 1 then mono-advance-to s p 0 0
    else if c == 2 then mono-advance-to s p 24 0
    else if c == 3 then mono-advance-to s p 11 0
    else if c <= 5 then mono-advance-to s p (mono-nearest (mono-pos s p) 8) 1
    else if c == 6 then mono-advance-to s p (mono-nearest (mono-pos s p) 9) 2
    else if c == 7 then mono-add-cash s p 50
    else if c == 9 then mono-back-three s p
    else if c == 10 then mono-to-jail s p
    else if c == 11 then mono-owe s p (-1) (mono-repairs s p 25 100)
    else if c == 12 then mono-owe s p (-1) 15
    else if c == 13 then mono-advance-to s p 5 0
    else if c == 14 then mono-pay-each s p 1
    else mono-add-cash s p 150

  mono-chest : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-chest (s) (p) (c) =
    if c == 0 then mono-advance-to s p 0 0
    else if c == 1 then mono-add-cash s p 200
    else if c == 2 then mono-owe s p (-1) 50
    else if c == 3 then mono-add-cash s p 50
    else if c == 5 then mono-to-jail s p
    else if c == 6 then mono-add-cash s p 100
    else if c == 7 then mono-add-cash s p 20
    else if c == 8 then mono-collect-each s p 1
    else if c == 9 then mono-add-cash s p 100
    else if c == 10 then mono-owe s p (-1) 100
    else if c == 11 then mono-owe s p (-1) 50
    else if c == 12 then mono-add-cash s p 25
    else if c == 13 then mono-owe s p (-1) (mono-repairs s p 40 115)
    else if c == 14 then mono-add-cash s p 10
    else mono-add-cash s p 100

  mono-back-three : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-back-three (s) (p) =
    let dest = mono-pos s p - 3
    in mono-land (mono-put s (mono-pslot p 0) dest) p dest 0

  mono-repairs : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-repairs (s) (p) (house) (hotel) = mono-repairs-loop s p house hotel 0 0

  mono-repairs-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-repairs-loop (s) (p) (house) (hotel) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then mono-repairs-loop s p house hotel (pi + 1) acc
    else let h = mono-houses s pi
    in let cost = if h == 5 then hotel else h * house
    in mono-repairs-loop s p house hotel (pi + 1) (acc + cost)

  mono-pay-each : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-pay-each (s) (p) (k) =
    if k >= mono-players s then s
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (mono-players s)
    in let s2 = if mono-out s q then s else mono-owe s p q 50
    in mono-pay-each s2 p (k + 1)

  mono-collect-each : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-collect-each (s) (p) (k) =
    if k >= mono-players s then s
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (mono-players s)
    in let s2 = if mono-out s q then s else mono-owe s q p 10
    in mono-collect-each s2 p (k + 1)

Section: Carrying On

 After a landing or an answer, the turn goes on in this order: debts are
 paid, the Bank's deeds are auctioned, a move owed from Jail is made, a
 doubles throw is thrown again, and otherwise the turn passes.

  mono-continue : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-continue (s) =
    if mono-over s then s
    else if mono-debts s > 0 then mono-settle s
    else if mono-aq s > 0 then mono-auction-next s (mono-get s (mono-aq-at + 1))
    else let p = mono-cur s
    in let owed = mono-get s mono-f-move
    in if mono-out s p then mono-end-turn s
    else if owed > 0 then mono-after (mono-move-by (mono-put (mono-set-phase s 0) mono-f-move 0) p owed)
    else if mono-get s mono-f-again == 1 then mono-set-phase (mono-put s mono-f-again 0) 0
    else mono-end-turn s

  mono-auction-next : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-auction-next (s) (pi) = mono-start-auction (mono-aq-pop s) pi

  mono-settle : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-settle (s) =
    let d = mono-debt s 0 0
    in let c = mono-debt s 0 1
    in let amt = mono-debt s 0 2
    in if mono-out s d then mono-continue (mono-debt-pop s)
    else if c >= 0 & mono-out s c then mono-continue (mono-debt-pop s)
    else if mono-cash s d >= amt then mono-continue (mono-debt-pop (mono-add-cash (mono-add-cash s d (0 - amt)) c amt))
    else mono-set-phase s 4

  mono-end-turn : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-end-turn (s) =
    let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-cur (mono-next-seat s (mono-cur s))) mono-f-turn (mono-get s mono-f-turn + 1)) mono-f-doubles 0
    in let s3 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-f-again 0) mono-f-pending (-1)) mono-f-move 0
    in mono-set-phase (mono-clear-asked s3 0) 0

  mono-clear-asked : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-clear-asked (s) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then s
    else mono-clear-asked (mono-put s (mono-dslot pi 3) 0) (pi + 1)

Section: Buying And Auctions

  mono-buy : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-buy (s) (p) =
    let pi = mono-get s mono-f-pending
    in let s2 = mono-put (mono-add-cash s p (0 - mono-price pi)) (mono-dslot pi 0) p
    in mono-continue (mono-set-phase (mono-put s2 mono-f-pending (-1)) 0)

  mono-active : MonopolyState, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-active (s) (p) = mono-get s (70 + p) == 1

  mono-start-auction : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-start-auction (s) (pi) =
    let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-pending (-1)) mono-f-aprop pi) mono-f-ahigh 0) mono-f-alead (-1)
    in let s3 = mono-seat-bidders s2 0
    in let first = if mono-active s3 (mono-cur s3) then mono-cur s3 else mono-next-bidder s3 (mono-cur s3)
    in mono-set-phase (mono-put s3 mono-f-aact first) 3

  mono-seat-bidders : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-seat-bidders (s) (p) =
    if p >= 4 then s
    else let live = if p < mono-players s then (if mono-out s p then 0 else 1) else 0
    in mono-seat-bidders (mono-put s (70 + p) live) (p + 1)

  mono-next-bidder : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-next-bidder (s) (p) = mono-next-bidder-loop s p 1

  mono-next-bidder-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-next-bidder-loop (s) (p) (k) =
    if k > mono-players s then (-1)
    else let q = rng-mod (p + k) (mono-players s)
    in if mono-active s q then q
    else mono-next-bidder-loop s p (k + 1)

  mono-bidders : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-bidders (s) (p) (acc) =
    if p >= 4 then acc
    else mono-bidders s (p + 1) (acc + mono-get s (70 + p))

  mono-bid : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-bid (s) (p) (amt) =
    let s2 = mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-ahigh amt) mono-f-alead p
    in let next = mono-next-bidder s2 p
    in if next == p then mono-end-auction s2
    else mono-put s2 mono-f-aact next

  mono-drop : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-drop (s) (p) =
    let s2 = mono-put s (70 + p) 0
    in let n = mono-bidders s2 0 0
    in let next = mono-next-bidder s2 p
    in if n == 0 then mono-end-auction s2
    else if n == 1 & next == mono-get s2 mono-f-alead then mono-end-auction s2
    else mono-put s2 mono-f-aact next

  mono-end-auction : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-end-auction (s) =
    let w = mono-get s mono-f-alead
    in let pi = mono-get s mono-f-aprop
    in let s2 = if w >= 0 then mono-put (mono-add-cash s w (0 - mono-get s mono-f-ahigh)) (mono-dslot pi 0) w else s
    in let s3 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-f-aprop (-1)) mono-f-ahigh 0) mono-f-alead (-1)) mono-f-aact (-1)
    in mono-continue (mono-set-phase (mono-seat-bidders-off s3 0) 0)

  mono-seat-bidders-off : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-seat-bidders-off (s) (p) =
    if p >= 4 then s
    else mono-seat-bidders-off (mono-put s (70 + p) 0) (p + 1)

Section: Buildings And Mortgages

  mono-build : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-build (s) (p) (pi) =
    let h = mono-houses s pi
    in let s2 = if h == 4 then mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-hotels (mono-get s mono-f-hotels - 1)) mono-f-houses (mono-get s mono-f-houses + 4) else mono-put s mono-f-houses (mono-get s mono-f-houses - 1)
    in mono-put (mono-add-cash s2 p (0 - mono-house-cost pi)) (mono-dslot pi 1) (h + 1)

  mono-sell : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-sell (s) (p) (pi) =
    let h = mono-houses s pi
    in let half = mono-house-cost pi / 2
    in if h == 5 then mono-sell-hotel s p pi half
    else mono-put (mono-add-cash (mono-put s mono-f-houses (mono-get s mono-f-houses + 1)) p half) (mono-dslot pi 1) (h - 1)

  mono-sell-hotel : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-sell-hotel (s) (p) (pi) (half) =
    let bank = mono-get s mono-f-houses
    in let got = if bank < 4 then bank else 4
    in let s2 = mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-hotels (mono-get s mono-f-hotels + 1)) mono-f-houses (bank - got)
    in mono-put (mono-add-cash s2 p (half * (5 - got))) (mono-dslot pi 1) got

  mono-mortgage : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-mortgage (s) (p) (pi) =
    mono-put (mono-add-cash s p (mono-mortgage-value pi)) (mono-dslot pi 2) 1

  mono-lift : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-lift (s) (p) (pi) =
    mono-put (mono-add-cash s p (0 - mono-lift-cost pi)) (mono-dslot pi 2) 0

Section: Bankruptcy

  mono-bankrupt : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-bankrupt (s) (d) (c) =
    let s1 = mono-drop-debts s d
    in let s2 = if c >= 0 then mono-cede-cash (mono-cede-to s1 d c 0) d c else mono-cede-cards (mono-cede-bank s1 d 0) d
    in let s3 = mono-put (mono-put s2 (mono-pslot d 6) 1) (mono-pslot d 1) 0
    in let s4 = if d == mono-cur s3 then mono-put (mono-put s3 mono-f-move 0) mono-f-again 0 else s3
    in mono-check-over s4

  mono-cede-to : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-cede-to (s) (d) (c) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then s
    else if mono-owner s pi /= d then mono-cede-to s d c (pi + 1)
    else let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-strip s d pi) (mono-dslot pi 0) c) (mono-dslot pi 3) 0
    in let s3 = if mono-mortgaged s2 pi then mono-owe s2 c (-1) (mono-interest pi) else s2
    in mono-cede-to s3 d c (pi + 1)

 The buildings on a bankrupt's lot go back to the Bank, which pays half
 their price to the bankrupt on the way to the creditor.

  mono-strip : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-strip (s) (d) (pi) =
    let h = mono-houses s pi
    in let s2 = if h == 5 then mono-put s mono-f-hotels (mono-get s mono-f-hotels + 1) else mono-put s mono-f-houses (mono-get s mono-f-houses + h)
    in mono-put (mono-add-cash s2 d (h * (mono-house-cost pi / 2))) (mono-dslot pi 1) 0

  mono-cede-cash : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-cede-cash (s) (d) (c) =
    let s2 = mono-add-cash s c (mono-cash s d)
    in let s3 = mono-put s2 (mono-pslot c 4) (mono-cards s2 c 0 + mono-cards s2 d 0)
    in let s4 = mono-put s3 (mono-pslot c 5) (mono-cards s3 c 1 + mono-cards s3 d 1)
    in mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s4 (mono-pslot d 1) 0) (mono-pslot d 4) 0) (mono-pslot d 5) 0

  mono-cede-bank : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-cede-bank (s) (d) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then s
    else if mono-owner s pi /= d then mono-cede-bank s d (pi + 1)
    else let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put (mono-strip s d pi) (mono-dslot pi 0) (-1)) (mono-dslot pi 2) 0) (mono-dslot pi 3) 0
    in mono-cede-bank (mono-aq-push s2 pi) d (pi + 1)

  mono-cede-cards : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-cede-cards (s) (d) =
    let s2 = if mono-cards s d 0 > 0 then mono-deck-bottom s 0 (mono-goojf 0) else s
    in let s3 = if mono-cards s2 d 1 > 0 then mono-deck-bottom s2 1 (mono-goojf 1) else s2
    in mono-put (mono-put s3 (mono-pslot d 4) 0) (mono-pslot d 5) 0

  mono-check-over : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-check-over (s) =
    if mono-live-count s 0 0 > 1 then s
    else let s2 = mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-over 1) mono-f-winner (mono-first-live s 0)) mono-debt-at 0
    in mono-set-phase (mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-aq-at 0) mono-f-move 0) 5

Section: Trading

 The engine's own players trade for a whole colour group: the one deed of
 a colour a player lacks, from the player holding it, for the one deed
 that completes the seller's own colour when there is one and otherwise
 for twice its printed price, keeping 150 back. A deed is asked for once a
 turn, a mortgaged deed never, and a trade with the person is an offer
 they answer.

  mono-trade-want : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-trade-want (s) (p) (g) =
    if mono-group-held s p g /= mono-group-size g - 1 then (-1)
    else mono-trade-want-loop s p g 0

  mono-trade-want-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-trade-want-loop (s) (p) (g) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then (-1)
    else if mono-group pi /= g then mono-trade-want-loop s p g (pi + 1)
    else if mono-owner s pi == p then mono-trade-want-loop s p g (pi + 1)
    else let q = mono-owner s pi
    in if q < 0 then (-1)
    else if mono-out s q then (-1)
    else if mono-mortgaged s pi then (-1)
    else if mono-asked s pi then (-1)
    else pi

  mono-trade-give : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-trade-give (s) (p) (want) =
    mono-trade-give-loop s p (mono-owner s want) (mono-group want) 0

  mono-trade-give-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-trade-give-loop (s) (p) (q) (skip) (g) =
    if g >= 8 then (-1)
    else if g == skip then mono-trade-give-loop s p q skip (g + 1)
    else if mono-group-held s q g /= mono-group-size g - 1 then mono-trade-give-loop s p q skip (g + 1)
    else let d = mono-other-deed s q g 0
    in if d < 0 then mono-trade-give-loop s p q skip (g + 1)
    else if mono-owner s d /= p then mono-trade-give-loop s p q skip (g + 1)
    else if mono-mortgaged s d then mono-trade-give-loop s p q skip (g + 1)
    else d

  mono-other-deed : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-other-deed (s) (q) (g) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then (-1)
    else if mono-group pi /= g then mono-other-deed s q g (pi + 1)
    else if mono-owner s pi == q then mono-other-deed s q g (pi + 1)
    else pi

  mono-trade-price : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-trade-price (s) (p) (want) =
    if mono-trade-give s p want >= 0 then 0 else 2 * mono-price want

  mono-trade-reserve : Integer
  mono-trade-reserve = 150

  mono-trade-ok : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  mono-trade-ok (s) (p) (want) =
    if mono-deed-ok want == False then False
    else let g = mono-group want
    in if g >= 8 then False
    else if mono-trade-want s p g /= want then False
    else if mono-trade-give s p want >= 0 then True
    else mono-cash s p >= 2 * mono-price want + mono-trade-reserve

  mono-trade : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-trade (s) (p) (want) =
    let q = mono-owner s want
    in let give = mono-trade-give s p want
    in let price = mono-trade-price s p want
    in let s2 = mono-put s (mono-dslot want 3) 1
    in if q == mono-get s mono-f-human then mono-set-phase (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s2 mono-f-twant want) mono-f-tgive give) mono-f-tprice price) 2
    else mono-swap s2 p q want give price

  mono-swap : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-swap (s) (p) (q) (want) (give) (price) =
    let s2 = mono-put s (mono-dslot want 0) p
    in if give >= 0 then mono-put s2 (mono-dslot give 0) q
    else mono-add-cash (mono-add-cash s2 p (0 - price)) q price

  mono-accept : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-accept (s) =
    let want = mono-get s mono-f-twant
    in let q = mono-owner s want
    in mono-clear-offer (mono-swap s (mono-cur s) q want (mono-get s mono-f-tgive) (mono-get s mono-f-tprice))

  mono-clear-offer : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mono-clear-offer (s) =
    mono-set-phase (mono-put (mono-put (mono-put s mono-f-twant (-1)) mono-f-tgive (-1)) mono-f-tprice 0) 0

Section: The Engine's Players

 A choice is one action packed as kind + 16 * player + 64 * argument, or -1
 when nobody has one. The engine's players buy what they can afford, bid up
 to a deed's price keeping 50 back, raise a debt by selling buildings and
 then mortgaging in board order, trade for a colour group before throwing,
 lift a mortgage keeping 400 back, build evenly keeping 300 back, and leave
 Jail early while six or more deeds are unowned.

  mono-code : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-code (kind) (p) (arg) = kind + 16 * p + 64 * arg

  mono-code-kind : Integer -> Integer
  mono-code-kind (c) = rng-mod c 16

  mono-code-player : Integer -> Integer
  mono-code-player (c) = rng-mod (c / 16) 4

  mono-code-arg : Integer -> Integer
  mono-code-arg (c) = c / 64

  mono-ai : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-ai (s) =
    let ph = mono-phase s
    in let p = mono-actor s
    in if mono-over s then (-1)
    else if p < 0 then (-1)
    else if ph == 0 then mono-ai-turn s p
    else if ph == 1 then (if mono-legal s p 1 0 then mono-code 1 p 0 else mono-code 2 p 0)
    else if ph == 2 then (if mono-get s mono-f-tgive >= 0 then mono-code 12 p 0 else mono-code 13 p 0)
    else if ph == 3 then mono-ai-bid s p
    else if ph == 4 then mono-ai-raise s p
    else (-1)

  mono-unowned : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-unowned (s) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else mono-unowned s (pi + 1) (acc + (if mono-owner s pi < 0 then 1 else 0))

  mono-ai-turn : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-turn (s) (p) =
    if mono-legal s p 10 0 then mono-code 10 p 0
    else if mono-legal s p 9 0 & mono-cash s p >= 250 & mono-unowned s 0 0 >= 6 then mono-code 9 p 0
    else let w = mono-ai-trade s p 0
    in if w >= 0 then mono-code 14 p w
    else let m = mono-ai-find s p 8 400 0
    in if m >= 0 then mono-code 8 p m
    else let b = mono-ai-find s p 5 300 0
    in if b >= 0 then mono-code 5 p b
    else mono-code 0 p 0

  mono-ai-trade : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-trade (s) (p) (g) =
    if g >= 8 then (-1)
    else let w = mono-trade-want s p g
    in if w >= 0 & mono-trade-ok s p w then w
    else mono-ai-trade s p (g + 1)

 The first deed in board order where the action is legal and leaves the
 player at least `keep` after its cost; a sale or a mortgage keeps nothing.

  mono-ai-cost : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-cost (kind) (pi) =
    if kind == 5 then mono-house-cost pi
    else if kind == 8 then mono-lift-cost pi
    else 0

  mono-ai-find : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-find (s) (p) (kind) (keep) (pi) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then (-1)
    else if mono-legal s p kind pi & mono-cash s p - mono-ai-cost kind pi >= keep then pi
    else mono-ai-find s p kind keep (pi + 1)

  mono-ai-bid : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-bid (s) (p) =
    let price = mono-price (mono-get s mono-f-aprop)
    in let room = mono-cash s p - 50
    in let limit = if room < price then room else price
    in let next = mono-get s mono-f-ahigh + 10
    in if next <= limit then mono-code 3 p next else mono-code 4 p 0

  mono-ai-raise : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-ai-raise (s) (p) =
    let sell = mono-ai-find s p 6 0 0
    in if sell >= 0 then mono-code 6 p sell
    else let m = mono-ai-find s p 7 0 0
    in if m >= 0 then mono-code 7 p m
    else mono-code 11 p 0

Section: Stepping

 A step plays the engine's choices until the turn passes, the game ends,
 or the choice falls to the person when it did not start with them.

  mono-step : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-step (s) (seed) =
    if mono-over s then s
    else mono-step-in (mono-copy s) seed

  mono-step-in : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mono-step-in (s) (seed) =
    let human = mono-get s mono-f-human
    in mono-step-loop s seed 0 (mono-get s mono-f-turn) (mono-actor s == human)

  mono-step-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> MonopolyState
  mono-step-loop (s) (seed) (n) (turn) (theirs) =
    if mono-over s then s
    else if n >= 400 then s
    else if (n > 0) & (mono-get s mono-f-turn /= turn) then s
    else if (n > 0) & (theirs == False) & (mono-actor s == mono-get s mono-f-human) then s
    else let code = mono-ai s
    in if code < 0 then s
    else let kind = mono-code-kind code
    in let p = mono-code-player code
    in let arg = if kind == 0 then seed + n * 7919 else mono-code-arg code
    in if mono-legal s p kind arg == False then s
    else mono-step-loop (mono-act-in s p kind arg) seed (n + 1) turn theirs

Section: Worth And The Turn Cap

  mono-worth : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mono-worth (s) (p) = mono-cash s p + mono-worth-loop s p 0 0

  mono-worth-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-worth-loop (s) (p) (pi) (acc) =
    if pi >= mono-deeds then acc
    else if mono-owner s pi /= p then mono-worth-loop s p (pi + 1) acc
    else let deed = if mono-mortgaged s pi then mono-price pi / 2 else mono-price pi
    in mono-worth-loop s p (pi + 1) (acc + deed + mono-houses s pi * mono-house-cost pi)

  mono-richest : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mono-richest (s) = mono-richest-loop s 0 (-1) (-1)

  mono-richest-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mono-richest-loop (s) (p) (best) (who) =
    if p >= mono-players s then who
    else if mono-out s p then mono-richest-loop s (p + 1) best who
    else let w = mono-worth s p
    in if w > best then mono-richest-loop s (p + 1) w p
    else mono-richest-loop s (p + 1) best who

  mono-turn-cap : Integer
  mono-turn-cap = 600

Section: Game Runner

  run-monopoly-game : Integer, Integer -> MonopolyResult
  run-monopoly-game (seed) (num-players) =
    mono-loop (mono-init seed num-players) seed 0

  mono-loop : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> MonopolyResult
  mono-loop (s) (seed) (n) =
    if mono-over s then mono-make-result s
    else if mono-get s mono-f-turn >= mono-turn-cap then mono-make-result s
    else if n > 20000 then mono-make-result s
    else mono-loop (mono-step-in s (seed * 7919 + n * 104729)) seed (n + 1)

  mono-make-result : MonopolyState -> MonopolyResult
  mono-make-result (s) =
    let w = if mono-over s then mono-get s mono-f-winner else mono-richest s
    in MonopolyResult { winner = w, turns = mono-get s mono-f-turn, final-cash = mono-collect-cash s 0 [] }

  mono-collect-cash : MonopolyState, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mono-collect-cash (s) (p) (acc) =
    if p >= mono-players s then acc
    else mono-collect-cash s (p + 1) (list-push acc (mono-cash s p))

Section: Formatting

  format-monopoly-result : MonopolyResult -> Text
  format-monopoly-result (r) =
    let w = if r.winner < 0 then "None" else "P" & show (r.winner + 1)
    in "Monopoly (" & show r.turns & " turns): winner=" & w

